{
  "description": "Listed Building Consent for internal alterations and refurbishment of Flat 9, a third-floor (attic storey) flat within a Grade II listed building. The works comprise: strip-out and replacement of the kitchen in its existing layout, including a small extension of a 1980s partition to reduce the kitchen doorway from a double door to a single door; refitting of the principal en-suite and family bathroom within their existing rooms; extension of the existing hallway cylinder cupboard, with new double doors in place of the existing single door, to house a replacement hot water cylinder and the condensing unit of a new, fully internal water-cooled comfort cooling system serving two new wall-mounted units in the reception room and principal bedroom; like-for-like replacement of the boiler in its existing position; new engineered oak flooring laid as a floating floor on acoustic underlay over the existing floors; internal shutters to the windows of the principal bedroom and Bedroom 2; new and replacement recessed downlights, additional sockets and lighting points, and upgraded bathroom extract fans ducted to the existing terminals; and redecoration throughout. No changes to the external elevations and no external plant are proposed. The proposals are described in full in the accompanying Heritage, Design and Access Statement and drawings.",
